30,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Midori,,I'm worried. I found that our joint clinics often fail because no one wants to take ownership of the budget or the rota.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I found that the call-back trial actually worked for elderly patients, but the benefits vanished the moment we stopped. We cannot just start and stop.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The staffing situation is precarious. Ward nursing is heavily reliant on agency cover, but the midwifery team actually has some breathing room.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The budget is a disaster. It's been cut by a quarter, and we're paying for floor space out of it. We cannot afford anything that doesn't generate revenue.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,Oh dear. I've found that our rooms and parking are already quite full. I worry we are trying to fit a large cake into a tiny box.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, if we choose a program that relies on outside bodies, we might save on space, but my findings show those agreements take forever to sign.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"If we ignore the evidence of what works—like the call-backs—we are just guessing. We need a program that is sustainable, not just cheap.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"We can't put more pressure on the ward nurses. If we choose a program, it must be one that the midwifery or therapy teams can absorb.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Midori, off-site work is a financial trap. I've seen the tariffs; we earn nothing if we aren't on-site. We need a program that brings patients here.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"But @Shion, if we bring more people here, where will they park? The shuttle only reaches a few villages. Our poor patients will be very stressed.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,It seems we are stuck between a lack of space and a lack of reliable partnerships. We need a program that is self-contained within a stable department.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. The data shows that consistency is the only thing that improves patient outcomes. A small, stable program is better than a large, failing one.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"Exactly. If we pick a program that lands on the ward nurses, it will just lead to more burnout and more agency costs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Then the logic is simple. We need a program that uses existing on-site space, utilizes the under-used midwifery or therapy staff, and maximizes the regional tariff.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I just hope the booking system can handle it. I found that so much of our work isn't even recorded. We might be busier than we think.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,"Let's look at the candidates with these constraints in mind. We must avoid ""joint"" programs that lack a clear owner.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"And we must avoid programs that are merely ""trials"" destined to be buried.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I will vote for whatever puts the least amount of stress on the ward staff.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,I will vote for the one that is financially viable. I won't support a program that leaves us unfunded in twelve months.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I shall vote for the one that doesn't make our hallways too crowded. Let's be gentle with our resources.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
