59,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I'm very concerned about Candidate D. It's a joint program between midwifery and pediatrics. Based on the board minutes, these often collapse.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Candidate A mirrors the call-back trial. I know it works for patients, but we must ensure it doesn't just ""stop"" when the budget runs out.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Candidate A would likely fall on the ward nurses, who are already exhausted and relying on agency cover. I cannot support that.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Candidate A is a financial disaster. Home visits draw no regional tariff. We would be paying staff to travel for zero revenue. It's illogical.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Candidate B requires a ""dedicated space."" My findings show our rooms are already full. I fear we have no place to put a new unit.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Midori,,Candidate C involves providers outside the hospital. My research shows those data agreements take over a year to sign. It would be a nightmare to start.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"If we reject A, B, and C, we are left with D. While joint programs are risky, the midwifery staff are actually available, according to Misaki.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Misaki,,That is true. The midwifery rota has slack. Candidate D is the only one that doesn't risk burning out the ward nurses or the therapy team.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"Candidate D is on-site, which means we get the regional tariff. It uses the available midwifery staff. It is the only option that makes financial sense.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"I am still worried about the parking and the booking system for Candidate D. But if it uses existing midwifery rooms, it might just fit.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I still worry about the ""joint"" nature of Candidate D. However, if we ensure one department holds the budget line, we can avoid the previous failures.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"The evidence for A was strong, but the operational constraints are too high. D is a compromise that we can actually sustain.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I feel comfortable with D. It aligns with the staffing surplus in midwifery and protects the ward nurses from more work.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"It is the only choice. A is a loss-leader, B is a space-hog, and C is a bureaucratic void. D is the only one that earns money and fits the staff.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"If you all agree, I will support it too. I will just ask the administration to be very careful with the booking slots so we don't overwhelm the lobby.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree. Let's go with Candidate D, but with a strict agreement on who manages the rota.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I can support that. It is better to have a sustainable program than a perfect one that is buried in a year.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree.,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,"Finally, a logical conclusion.","{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shizue,,Let us hope it brings joy to the new parents without causing too much traffic in the car park.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
